---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Geary"
  description="Privacy Policy for Geary: zero accounts, zero tracking cookies, and client-side search."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 sm:py-10 lg:px-8 lg:py-12">
    <div class="mb-8 border-b border-border-subtle pb-6 max-w-[65ch]">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { label: 'Privacy Policy' },
        ]}
      />

      <h1 class="font-heading text-[1.75rem] sm:text-[2.25rem] font-bold leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink-primary">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-3 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-secondary">
        How Geary handles data: static pages, client-side search, and zero personal tracking.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 text-xs font-medium text-ink-secondary">
        Effective Date: November 19, 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    <article class="geary-prose">
      <h2>1. Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Geary is a purely static student information website. You do not need an account to read any article, and we design the site to collect as little data as technically possible.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Geary does <strong>not</strong> ask for, collect, store, or sell personal information. Specifically:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>No user accounts, logins, or student number inputs.</li>
        <li>No Geary-operated comment sections or submission databases.</li>
        <li>No Geary-set advertising trackers, behavioral profiling, or tracking cookies.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        On the optional <a href="/contribute">Contribute</a> page, Geary embeds a third-party Google Form with email collection and sign-in limits turned off. Loading that <code>docs.google.com</code> form connects your browser directly to Google under Google&apos;s own privacy policy. Any contributor credit name or follow-up contact you voluntarily enter is reviewed solely by Geary maintainers to attribute credit or ask clarification questions, and is never sold or shared for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Client-Side Search, Campus Map &amp; Daily Rotation</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the search bar, your browser downloads a static JSON file (<code>/search-index.json</code>) containing article titles, headings, and summaries. All filtering and ranking run locally inside your browser; your search terms are never sent to a Geary server or stored by us.
      </p>
      <p>
        The interactive <a href="/map">Main Campus map</a> and the Home page&apos;s daily rotating Featured section also run entirely in your browser using static files and your device&apos;s local calendar date. Geary never requests GPS or browser geolocation permissions.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Hosting &amp; Standard Server Logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like any static website on the internet, the hosting provider serving Geary’s files may automatically record standard HTTP request logs (such as IP address, browser user-agent, requested path, and timestamp) to maintain uptime, prevent abuse, and serve pages securely. Geary does not use these logs to identify individual students.
      </p>

      <h2>5. External Links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles frequently reference or link to official BulSU portals, university and student council Facebook pages, Google Forms, and external resources. Once you leave Geary, those third-party platforms operate under their own privacy practices and terms.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Updates to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        If Geary ever introduces optional features that process user data or analytics, this Privacy Policy will be updated before those changes take effect.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
